WEBVTT

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.936
You're late.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.103
There was a problem

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.170
with the pulse drills
on Level 4.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.909
They're going to be
here any moment.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.507
I want to make a
good impression.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.780
You're certain
we should be doing this?

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.652
Orek will be pleased that
we took the initiative.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.883
Oh. I hope you're right.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.558
Welcome to Telsius.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.599
Thank you.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.691
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.361
This is Commander Tuvok.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.600
We're from the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.416
We have several mines
like this on Earth.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.214
I'm not familiar with Earth.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:38.087
That's because it's 30,000
light-years from here.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:42.094
30,342.4, to be exact.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:44.221
You're a long way from home.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.924
It's difficult sometimes.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.899
Then I close my eyes and think

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.629
of the farm in Indiana,
where I grew up,

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.297
and for a moment,
I'm home again.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.967
Shall we get down to business?

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.202
Yes.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.938
Uh, we've had a shortage
of dilithium

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.274
for the last two months.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.507
If we can't
replenish our supply,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.142
we may be forced
to suspend work.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:08.619
Our Chief of Mining
Operations has gone

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.814
to the Grenna system...

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.550
Yeah, but, um, we
are authorized

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.785
to conduct trades
in his absence.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.420
What are you prepared to trade?

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.829
I'm afraid the only commodity

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.834
we have is, uh, bolomite.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:29.069
We really don't have
much use for that.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.939
On the contrary, Captain.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.446
Bolomite is used in
omega radiation therapy.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.606
The orphans on Narva...

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.207
Orphans?

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.945
The settlers
on the Narva Colony

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.748
were exposed to toxic levels
of omega radiation.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:47.384
The entire adult population...
was killed.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:51.328
We're doing all we can
for the children.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.365
All right.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.594
20 kilotons of dilithium

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.465
for an equivalent amount
of bolomite.

00:03:57.537 --> 00:04:00.904
We only have ten kilotons left.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:02.498
Then ten it is.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.837
Captain, I must point out

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.572
that dilithium is worth
nearly twice as much

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.375
as bolomite.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:09.915
Tuvok, these people
need our help.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.177
I'm not going to quibble

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.344
over a few tons of ore.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.081
Perhaps we should celebrate.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.452
I wish we could, but there's

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.320
a neutronic storm
approaching our ship.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.916
We should be
leaving orbit.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.893
Um, give us an hour
to finalize the arrangements.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.557
We'll be waiting
to hear from you.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:30.433
Before we leave, would it be
possible to tour your facility?

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.733
It's our duty
as Starfleet officers to...

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.399
Unfortunately,
the storm won't wait.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.272
Maybe on our next visit.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.948
Live long and prosper.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.948
Oh, this hair
is so uncomfortable.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.287
I find it
aesthetically pleasing.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.353
The negotiations?

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.523
It would've been perfect

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.226
if "Tuvok" hadn't decided
to improvise.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.563
I was portraying my character

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.899
as truthfully as possible.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.495
Once we finish a
transaction, we leave.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.597
Is that clear?

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.869
Indeed.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.173
Incoming transmission

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:17.216
for Captain Janeway.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.454
Ready.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.624
This is Captain Janeway.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.428
The bolomite is
ready for transport.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.092
We thank you for
your generosity.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:39.832
Directive 927 of the
Starfleet General Order:

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.136
"Always help those in need."

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.274
Transport complete.

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.336
We've enjoyed
meeting you, gentlemen.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:52.680
Uh, Captain, uh, we haven't
received the dilithium yet.

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.379
Oh, the neutronic storm

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:56.945
seems to be interfering
with our transporters.

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:57.955
If we don't

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.115
leave orbit immediately

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.557
we will sustain heavy damage.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:03.390
What about our dilithium?

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.693
We'll be back to deliver it
as soon as the storm clears.

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.130
Well, how long will that be?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.758
Captain Janeway out.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:11.660
Let's go.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:29.355
Computer, activate
the sonic shower.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.553
Oh...

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.821
adjust the frequency.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:41.197
Whew! Computer, deactivate
the sonic shower!

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:55.580
Report.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:59.311
We've got systems failures
on eight decks, Captain.

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:00.943
That explains why
my sonic shower

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.611
was a little
louder than usual.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:03.882
Make that nine decks.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:05.615
I've run every
diagnostic I know,

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.716
and I can't seem to
isolate the problem.

00:07:07.794 --> 00:07:08.783
Gremlins.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.055
Excuse me?

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:12.757
In the early days
of aviation, engineers blamed

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:15.266
imaginary little creatures
called gremlins

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.802
for malfunctions
they could not explain.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.662
Well, one of your gremlins

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.334
just paid a visit to
the replicator system.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:33.608
Tuvok, we saved you a seat.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.555
What's wrong?

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:40.387
Someone has altered
one of my holodeck programs...

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.825
again.

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.362
Hmm. Are you sure it isn't
just one of these malfunctions?

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.193
Everything on the
ship's been affected,

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:47.357
including the holodecks.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.196
The Oracle of K'Tal

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:52.260
isn't programmed
to wear pajamas.

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:55.796
Well, maybe he overslept.

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:58.571
I am not amused by
your practical jokes, Mr. Paris.

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.737
Why do you
always think it's me?

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.508
Mr. Kim?

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:06.279
Mmm. I'd like to claim credit,
but I'm innocent.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:09.810
The next time I visit
the holodeck, I expect to find

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:13.017
my program restored
to its original parameters.

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:16.493
I'm telling you, Tuvok,
we didn't do it.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:19.588
I wonder how the Oracle
would look in a sombrero.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.092
Everybody, stop eating.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.160
Captain, what's wrong?

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:27.468
If I could have everyone's
attention for a moment.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.804
We found a contaminant
in the replicator system.

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:32.276
It's nothing serious,
but if any of you

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.279
start to feel a little queasy,

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.871
report to Sick Bay immediately.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.882
In the meantime,
the galley is closed.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.283
Wish I hadn't had seconds.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:46.652
Here.

00:08:55.635 --> 00:08:57.159
Well, that explains it.

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:58.203
Well, don't tell me

00:08:58.271 --> 00:09:00.068
a simple heating
coil in the stove

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:01.834
is responsible for everything

00:09:01.908 --> 00:09:03.705
that's gone wrong this morning.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:05.971
Any component connected
to the integrated circuitry

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.103
can spread
a contaminant.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:09.477
This isn't Starfleet issue.

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.016
Where did it come from?

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:13.574
I obtained it
during a trade.

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:14.711
With whom?

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:17.153
Sister Dala.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.520
"Sister"?

00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:20.889
One of the clerics
on Selnia Prime.

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:22.221
Tom and I met her

00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:23.762
during our away mission.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:24.761
She was the one

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.821
trying to help
all those poor orphans.

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:28.161
It's, it's,
it's all in our report.

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:29.701
Did you run a diagnostic
before you

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:30.633
installed it?

00:09:30.703 --> 00:09:32.330
Captain to the Bridge.

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:33.895
I'm a little busy now.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:34.997
Can it wait?

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:36.302
I'm afraid not.

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:37.933
I'll be right back.

00:09:42.782 --> 00:09:44.909
One excuse after another.

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:48.920
You're stalling,
and I don't have time for it.

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:51.388
Captain, this is Mr. Orek.

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:53.288
He's Chief of Mining Operations

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:54.792
on Telsius Prime.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.384
A problem, Mr. Orek?

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:58.327
Not if your deliver
our dilithium.

00:09:58.397 --> 00:09:59.921
Dilithium?

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:02.865
It's all clearly documented.

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:05.267
Ten kilotons of bolomite ore

00:10:05.338 --> 00:10:08.603
in exchange
for ten kilotons of dilithium.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:14.046
I think there's been
some sort of misunderstanding.

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:19.608
One way or another, I intend
to collect what you owe me.

00:10:25.091 --> 00:10:26.888
We've enjoyed meeting you,
gentlemen.

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:29.086
Uh, Captain,
uh, we haven't received

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:30.128
the dilithium yet.

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:32.824
Oh, the neutronic storm
seems to be interfering

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:34.092
with our transporters.

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:36.157
If we don't leave orbit
immediately,

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:38.066
we will sustain
heavy damage.

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:40.162
What about our dilithium?

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:43.299
We'll be back to deliver it
as soon as the storm clears.

00:10:44.944 --> 00:10:47.242
Do you still deny
you made the trade?

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:49.508
That woman isn't me.

00:10:49.582 --> 00:10:50.810
Who is she, then?

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:52.077
Well, she's
obviously an impostor.

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:55.314
I have transmission logs,
transport records,

00:10:55.388 --> 00:10:57.515
scans of your shuttlecraft.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.956
I have never been
to your planet, Mr. Orek,

00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:01.994
aboard Voyager
or any other vessel.

00:11:02.061 --> 00:11:03.926
Our ship's logs
will confirm what

00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:05.257
the Captain's been telling you.

00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:07.799
And how do I know
they're authentic records?

00:11:07.867 --> 00:11:10.301
How do we know your
records are authentic?

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:13.031
You think I falsified data?

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:15.073
Why would I do that?

00:11:15.141 --> 00:11:16.733
Perhaps to extort
dilithium from us.

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:18.834
I'm not the thief here.

00:11:18.911 --> 00:11:21.573
We are not questioning
your integrity, Mr. Orek.

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:23.547
It does appear
you've been cheated,

00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:25.811
but not by me or
anyone on my crew.

00:11:25.885 --> 00:11:28.479
How naive do you think I am?

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:31.250
First, you prey upon
the sympathy of my miners

00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:32.415
by telling them
stories

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:33.958
about poor,
orphaned children.

00:11:34.093 --> 00:11:37.529
Now you try to convince me
you're the victims here.

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:40.861
Did you say "orphaned children"?

00:11:40.933 --> 00:11:42.867
A despicable tactic.

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:45.733
Will you excuse me
for a minute, please?

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:50.071
We're not finished!

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:54.379
Neelix.

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:57.314
Captain, we're making
real progress with the...

00:11:57.383 --> 00:11:58.645
Never mind that.

00:11:58.718 --> 00:12:00.709
Tell me more
about this cleric

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:02.811
who gave you
the heating coil.

00:12:02.888 --> 00:12:04.321
Uh, Sister Dala?

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.483
What do you want to know?

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:07.924
Everything.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:11.086
Well, Tom and I met her
during our away mission.

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:14.360
We were on a small planetoid
in the Wyanti system,

00:12:14.433 --> 00:12:16.526
searching for a spore
the Doctor wanted

00:12:16.602 --> 00:12:18.331
to grow
antiviral proteins with.

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:21.339
I tell you, Neelix,
when I first joined Starfleet,

00:12:21.407 --> 00:12:22.840
I knew it was gonna

00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:25.376
be one glamorous
adventure after another,

00:12:25.444 --> 00:12:28.277
but I never dreamed that
I'd have the opportunity

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:30.338
to go on
a mold-hunting expedition.

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:33.180
I'm detecting traces of glamour

00:12:33.252 --> 00:12:34.685
in this direction.

00:12:34.754 --> 00:12:36.847
Please, go no further.

00:12:36.922 --> 00:12:39.049
This is our sanctuary.

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:40.922
Our scans didn't
detect anyone

00:12:40.993 --> 00:12:42.255
down here.

00:12:42.328 --> 00:12:43.920
Our sect is a solitary one.

00:12:43.996 --> 00:12:45.429
We dampen our life signs

00:12:45.498 --> 00:12:47.966
to protect the privacy
of our meditations.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.365
We're terribly sorry
if we've disturbed you.

00:12:51.437 --> 00:12:53.234
Begin the cleansing.

00:12:56.542 --> 00:12:59.978
Olat mal pri,
mal pra, mal prolat,

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:04.310
olate kal mi,
kal mal, kal molat.

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:06.510
I hope we
haven't committed

00:13:06.585 --> 00:13:08.553
a serious transgression.

00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:10.555
The transgression was ours.

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:13.217
We should have
guarded the sanctuary

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:14.782
more carefully.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.624
The Deities will be angry.

00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:18.924
Come on, Neelix.

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:20.498
We'd better get
out of the way.

00:13:20.566 --> 00:13:21.828
Of... of course.

00:13:21.901 --> 00:13:23.198
Our sincere apologies.

00:13:23.269 --> 00:13:25.464
L-if there's anything
we can do...

00:13:25.538 --> 00:13:30.339
Forgive me, but
you look familiar.

00:13:30.409 --> 00:13:34.675
I don't think that
we've ever met before.

00:13:34.747 --> 00:13:36.874
Do you see it?

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:39.550
Yes.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.151
You bear
a striking resemblance

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:46.953
to our Redeemer of Light.

00:13:47.026 --> 00:13:49.756
I'm flattered.

00:13:49.829 --> 00:13:52.423
Each spring, we make
a pilgrimage to Narva

00:13:52.498 --> 00:13:54.591
in his honor,
to help the orphans.

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:58.194
Well, that's a very
worthy cause.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.295
It is.

00:14:00.372 --> 00:14:05.332
Unfortunately, we have no food
to bring them this year.

00:14:05.411 --> 00:14:06.378
Why not?

00:14:06.445 --> 00:14:08.037
A blight infected

00:14:08.113 --> 00:14:10.047
our hydroponic pods.

00:14:10.115 --> 00:14:12.310
The crop was destroyed.

00:14:12.384 --> 00:14:15.547
Maybe we could replicate
some food for you.

00:14:15.621 --> 00:14:18.021
We bestow charity on others.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.887
The Deities forbid us

00:14:19.959 --> 00:14:21.824
from accepting it ourselves.

00:14:21.894 --> 00:14:23.327
How about a trade?

00:14:23.395 --> 00:14:24.828
Yeah. Good idea.

00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:26.797
You must have something
that we can use.

00:14:26.866 --> 00:14:28.925
That way, you wouldn't
be accepting charity,

00:14:29.068 --> 00:14:30.695
and the Deities
would have nothing

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:32.066
to get angry about.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:41.675
Your heart is as kind
as your face.

00:14:41.747 --> 00:14:45.239
May the Deities
bless you.

00:14:45.317 --> 00:14:47.046
That's when they

00:14:47.119 --> 00:14:48.848
gave you the heating coil?

00:14:48.921 --> 00:14:50.183
It was going to take a while

00:14:50.256 --> 00:14:51.951
to replicate the supplies
they needed,

00:14:52.091 --> 00:14:53.854
so we invited them back
to the Flyer.

00:14:53.926 --> 00:14:54.950
That's when
they must have

00:14:55.094 --> 00:14:56.288
gotten access to our systems.

00:14:56.362 --> 00:14:57.624
Captain?

00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:59.459
Did you leave either of them

00:14:59.531 --> 00:15:00.793
alone at any point?

00:15:00.866 --> 00:15:02.128
I don't think so.

00:15:02.201 --> 00:15:04.795
Uh, after we ate,
Tom took Brother Mobar

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.132
to see the cockpit,

00:15:06.205 --> 00:15:08.196
but I stayed
in the aft section

00:15:08.274 --> 00:15:09.901
with Sister Dala, talking.

00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:11.805
About what?

00:15:11.877 --> 00:15:14.277
Well, me, mostly.

00:15:14.346 --> 00:15:17.315
She wanted to know
all about my role on Voyager.

00:15:17.383 --> 00:15:20.284
Ambassador,
Morale Officer, Head Chef.

00:15:20.352 --> 00:15:23.321
It sounds as though
you're invaluable.

00:15:23.389 --> 00:15:25.323
I do what I can.

00:15:25.391 --> 00:15:27.825
Where is
your Voyager now?

00:15:27.893 --> 00:15:30.919
About three
light-years from here.

00:15:31.063 --> 00:15:33.759
Mmm. Your crew is alone
in this region?

00:15:33.832 --> 00:15:35.925
We are the only
Federation starship

00:15:36.001 --> 00:15:37.593
within 30,000 light-years.

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:39.501
That must be difficult.

00:15:39.571 --> 00:15:41.937
Sometimes it is, but we manage.

00:15:42.007 --> 00:15:44.908
We've single-handedly
taken on the Borg,

00:15:44.977 --> 00:15:47.138
the Hirogen, Species 8472...

00:15:47.212 --> 00:15:49.942
Oh. I'm impressed.

00:15:50.082 --> 00:15:52.642
Captain Janeway deserves
most of the credit.

00:15:52.718 --> 00:15:54.447
She's an extraordinary woman.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.613
Your Captain is a woman?

00:15:56.689 --> 00:15:58.782
The finest one I've ever known.

00:15:58.857 --> 00:16:00.620
Tell me about her.

00:16:00.693 --> 00:16:03.287
Well, uh...
she's commanded Voyager

00:16:03.362 --> 00:16:05.125
for almost six years now.

00:16:05.197 --> 00:16:07.631
Before that, she was a science
officer on the Al-Batani.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.565
Where does she come from?

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:10.829
Earth.

00:16:10.903 --> 00:16:12.598
It's in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:16:12.671 --> 00:16:13.899
She grew up on

00:16:14.006 --> 00:16:16.338
a little farm
in a place called Indiana.

00:16:16.408 --> 00:16:17.670
You'd like her.

00:16:17.743 --> 00:16:20.268
I'm sure I would.

00:16:20.346 --> 00:16:22.314
Sister Dala.

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:23.905
Yes, Brother Mobar.

00:16:24.049 --> 00:16:25.311
It's late.

00:16:25.384 --> 00:16:27.648
We must return
to the sanctuary.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.483
So soon?

00:16:29.555 --> 00:16:32.581
It's time for
the evening meditation.

00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:36.924
We can't thank you enough
for all you've done.

00:16:37.062 --> 00:16:39.929
We're just glad
that we could help.

00:16:40.065 --> 00:16:41.327
The blessing.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.698
Certainly.

00:16:49.742 --> 00:16:51.801
May the Deities

00:16:51.877 --> 00:16:54.345
bless these travelers.

00:16:54.413 --> 00:16:56.938
Tala ot val,

00:16:57.016 --> 00:17:00.042
tala ot relina,

00:17:00.119 --> 00:17:01.416
sen tala,

00:17:01.487 --> 00:17:03.079
sen relina,

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:04.782
val golina,

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:07.018
su ketran,

00:17:07.092 --> 00:17:08.525
tala otval,

00:17:08.594 --> 00:17:09.686
tala ot relina.

00:17:09.762 --> 00:17:11.195
Then we transported them

00:17:11.263 --> 00:17:12.628
back to their sanctuary.

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:15.428
How long did this blessing last?

00:17:15.501 --> 00:17:17.901
No more than a minute or two.

00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:20.801
That's probably all they needed.

00:17:20.873 --> 00:17:22.864
For what?

00:17:26.879 --> 00:17:28.813
Just what I thought.

00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:31.145
The entire database
was downloaded

00:17:31.216 --> 00:17:33.309
18 days ago.

00:17:33.385 --> 00:17:36.513
Brother Mobar... the talisman.

00:17:36.588 --> 00:17:37.714
It was obviously

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:38.722
some sort of scanner.

00:17:38.791 --> 00:17:39.723
What would a couple

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:40.781
of religious clerics

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:42.053
want with our database?

00:17:42.127 --> 00:17:44.220
It might help

00:17:44.296 --> 00:17:46.924
if they wanted to pose
as Federation officers.

00:17:47.066 --> 00:17:48.590
Gentlemen,

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:51.534
I believe you've been had.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:04.649
The way I see it,
we're both victims.

00:18:04.716 --> 00:18:06.616
Your bolomite was stolen,

00:18:06.685 --> 00:18:09.586
and our reputation
has been damaged.

00:18:09.655 --> 00:18:11.486
What are you proposing?

00:18:11.557 --> 00:18:14.321
You said you had
scans of the vessel

00:18:14.393 --> 00:18:16.224
that visited your mining colony.

00:18:16.295 --> 00:18:17.887
If you allow us to analyze them,

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.361
we might be able to derive

00:18:19.431 --> 00:18:21.023
the impostors' warp signature.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.068
We could find them
and recover your property

00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:24.500
before they cheat
someone else.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:28.233
This is all difficult
for me to believe.

00:18:28.307 --> 00:18:31.902
Two of your crewmen
deceived by clerics?

00:18:32.044 --> 00:18:35.445
Humph! Could they really
have been so naive?

00:18:35.514 --> 00:18:37.072
A legitimate question.

00:18:37.149 --> 00:18:39.049
It's obvious we're dealing

00:18:39.118 --> 00:18:40.142
with clever adversaries...

00:18:40.219 --> 00:18:41.186
they fooled both of us.

00:18:41.253 --> 00:18:42.720
But I'm confident
we can stop them.

00:18:42.788 --> 00:18:45.814
Perhaps I should
contact Telsian Security.

00:18:45.891 --> 00:18:48.257
They have,
uh, persuasive methods

00:18:48.327 --> 00:18:50.261
for determining the truth.

00:18:50.329 --> 00:18:53.196
In the meantime,
the real thieves

00:18:53.265 --> 00:18:55.756
could be halfway
across the sector,

00:18:55.834 --> 00:18:58.769
with your bolomite
in their cargo hold.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:20.783
And finally,
our Bridge.

00:19:20.859 --> 00:19:23.419
Is this a typical
Federation vessel?

00:19:23.495 --> 00:19:24.826
Well, the Delta Flyer

00:19:24.897 --> 00:19:25.829
may look a little worn,

00:19:25.898 --> 00:19:26.830
but that's only because

00:19:26.899 --> 00:19:28.025
she's been through so much.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.159
This ship
has helped fend off

00:19:30.235 --> 00:19:33.693
the Borg, the Hirogen,
Species 8472.

00:19:33.772 --> 00:19:37.003
Most of your technology
is outdated.

00:19:37.075 --> 00:19:39.703
Show him the mothership,
Mr. Chakotay.

00:19:39.778 --> 00:19:41.769
The USS Voyager...

00:19:41.847 --> 00:19:43.337
Intrepid-class.

00:19:43.415 --> 00:19:45.815
15 decks of the most
advanced technology

00:19:45.884 --> 00:19:47.146
you'll find anywhere.

00:19:47.219 --> 00:19:49.084
Dilithium-powered
warp engines,

00:19:49.154 --> 00:19:51.122
integrated
bio-neural circuitry,

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.852
holodecks...

00:19:53.926 --> 00:19:56.793
Is this a typical
Federation vessel?

00:19:56.862 --> 00:19:59.922
Every ship in the fleet is built
to exacting standards.

00:20:00.032 --> 00:20:01.727
But I'd be lying if I told you

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.927
I didn't think Voyager
was exceptional.

00:20:04.069 --> 00:20:07.129
As her Captain,
I'm not entirely objective.

00:20:07.206 --> 00:20:10.937
I'm sure you feel
the same way about your ship.

00:20:11.076 --> 00:20:13.943
It is my home.

00:20:14.079 --> 00:20:16.570
I'm glad to hear you
say that, Mr. Varn...

00:20:16.648 --> 00:20:23.315
because that's exactly
what the Federation is... a home

00:20:23.388 --> 00:20:27.119
for an extended family
who share resources

00:20:27.192 --> 00:20:31.424
and come to one another's aid
in time of need.

00:20:31.496 --> 00:20:34.056
So, if my ship joins
your Federation,

00:20:34.132 --> 00:20:36.965
Voyager will help
me fight my enemies?

00:20:37.102 --> 00:20:40.868
The primary goal of
the Federation is exploration.

00:20:40.939 --> 00:20:41.906
Military objectives are...

00:20:41.974 --> 00:20:43.271
There's no need

00:20:43.342 --> 00:20:46.311
to bore our guest
with Starfleet protocol, Tuvok.

00:20:46.378 --> 00:20:49.176
My enemies have
sophisticated weaponry.

00:20:49.248 --> 00:20:52.081
As do we.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:53.481
Photon torpedoes...

00:20:53.552 --> 00:20:57.989
optronically targeted phasers...

00:20:58.056 --> 00:20:59.990
multispectrum shielding.

00:21:00.058 --> 00:21:01.719
All of which

00:21:01.793 --> 00:21:03.658
we would not hesitate to share

00:21:03.729 --> 00:21:06.493
with a fellow member
of the Federation.

00:21:06.565 --> 00:21:08.726
What will I have to do to join?

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.631
In order to be considered,

00:21:10.702 --> 00:21:13.637
a candidate must make
formal application.

00:21:13.705 --> 00:21:16.538
An extensive review is conducted
by a committee composed of...

00:21:16.608 --> 00:21:18.439
The process is complicated,

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.842
but Captain Janeway
has influence

00:21:20.912 --> 00:21:22.846
with the Federation Council.

00:21:22.914 --> 00:21:26.213
And you would use that
influence on my behalf?

00:21:26.285 --> 00:21:29.220
Well, I'd be foolish not to.

00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:36.387
You are just the type
of candidate we're looking for.

00:21:36.461 --> 00:21:39.089
Uh, I'll have to discuss
this with my shipmates.

00:21:39.164 --> 00:21:42.292
Well, joining the Federation
is a serious commitment.

00:21:42.367 --> 00:21:43.959
Take all the time you need.

00:21:44.069 --> 00:21:47.095
Captain, our latest orders
from Starfleet Command.

00:21:47.172 --> 00:21:49.970
We won't be back here
for at least six months.

00:21:50.075 --> 00:21:52.669
Well, perhaps we can discuss
your application then.

00:21:52.744 --> 00:21:55.838
L-lf we were to apply now,

00:21:55.914 --> 00:21:58.246
could you assure us
we'd be accepted?

00:22:02.187 --> 00:22:06.089
You realize you'll have to
commit considerable resources?

00:22:06.158 --> 00:22:08.683
I'll do whatever is necessary.

00:22:10.495 --> 00:22:14.397
Well, let me be
the first to say...

00:22:14.466 --> 00:22:15.398
welcome

00:22:15.467 --> 00:22:17.662
to the Federation.

00:22:28.046 --> 00:22:30.640
You look like you could
use a cup of coffee.

00:22:30.716 --> 00:22:31.648
I've been flying

00:22:31.717 --> 00:22:33.082
concentric
search patterns

00:22:33.151 --> 00:22:35.483
for the last 12 hours.

00:22:35.554 --> 00:22:39.388
Any sign
of the impostors?

00:22:39.458 --> 00:22:42.723
Neelix, what has happened to us?

00:22:42.794 --> 00:22:45.160
I know exactly what you mean.

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:46.891
I've been over it
a thousand times.

00:22:46.965 --> 00:22:48.626
Why didn't we see this coming?

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:49.632
Orphans.

00:22:49.701 --> 00:22:51.692
It's the oldest gambit
in the book.

00:22:51.770 --> 00:22:54.500
I-I mean, if it'd been Harry,
I could understand it.

00:22:54.573 --> 00:22:56.541
He trusts everybody,
but you and me?

00:22:56.608 --> 00:22:59.304
We've dealt with our share
of shady characters.

00:23:00.345 --> 00:23:01.573
I think maybe...

00:23:01.646 --> 00:23:03.773
maybe we've lost our edge.

00:23:07.452 --> 00:23:10.444
Hand me one of those
terra nuts.

00:23:10.522 --> 00:23:11.784
What are you doing?

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:13.085
Proving you wrong.

00:23:13.158 --> 00:23:16.025
Ah, the old shell game.

00:23:16.094 --> 00:23:19.257
All we need
now is a mark.

00:23:19.331 --> 00:23:21.856
I think I see one coming.

00:23:21.933 --> 00:23:23.400
Uh, you go ahead.

00:23:23.468 --> 00:23:25.936
I'll follow your lead.

00:23:26.071 --> 00:23:27.561
Now, watch carefully.

00:23:27.639 --> 00:23:30.301
I place the terra nut
under the cup.

00:23:30.375 --> 00:23:31.808
Then I shuffle them.

00:23:31.877 --> 00:23:33.936
'Round and 'round they go.

00:23:34.079 --> 00:23:36.240
Keep your eye
on the nut.

00:23:36.314 --> 00:23:40.648
But be careful... the hand
is faster than the eye.

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:43.153
Now, for three hours
of holodeck time,

00:23:43.221 --> 00:23:45.815
can you tell me
where is the terra nut?

00:23:45.891 --> 00:23:46.858
Uh...

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:49.588
there.

00:23:49.661 --> 00:23:52.755
No, no... no,
that one.

00:23:52.831 --> 00:23:56.323
Oh... I really thought
I had you this time.

00:23:56.401 --> 00:23:58.426
Oh, keep trying, Neelix.

00:23:58.503 --> 00:23:59.970
You'll fool me
one of these days.

00:24:00.038 --> 00:24:01.130
This looks like
an interesting game.

00:24:01.206 --> 00:24:02.138
May I have a turn?

00:24:02.207 --> 00:24:03.139
Oh, be my guest.

00:24:03.208 --> 00:24:06.803
But, um, you'll have
to wager something.

00:24:06.878 --> 00:24:09.711
If I win, you take
three duty shifts in Sick Bay.

00:24:09.781 --> 00:24:14.343
And if I win, you take
three shifts in the Kitchen.

00:24:14.419 --> 00:24:16.011
Done.

00:24:16.087 --> 00:24:18.055
Ready?

00:24:18.123 --> 00:24:22.150
Now, watch carefully.

00:24:22.227 --> 00:24:23.660
'Round and 'round they go.

00:24:23.728 --> 00:24:25.696
Follow the terra nut if you can.

00:24:25.764 --> 00:24:27.629
But be careful...
the hand is faster

00:24:27.699 --> 00:24:28.631
than the eye.

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:30.759
Careful, Doc,
try not to blink.

00:24:30.836 --> 00:24:32.269
Don't you worry, Mr. Paris.

00:24:32.337 --> 00:24:34.828
You have to get up
pretty early in the morning

00:24:34.906 --> 00:24:36.567
to fool
my optical subroutines.

00:24:43.482 --> 00:24:44.972
Where is it, then?

00:24:46.051 --> 00:24:47.882
In your left palm.

00:24:54.726 --> 00:24:55.658
How did you?

00:24:55.727 --> 00:24:57.194
Superior visual acuity.

00:24:57.262 --> 00:24:58.559
See you in Sick Bay.

00:25:04.703 --> 00:25:07.171
I'm detecting a vessel
on long-range scans.

00:25:07.239 --> 00:25:10.072
The warp signature matches
the impostor's ship.

00:25:10.141 --> 00:25:12.371
Harry, tell Tom
his coffee break is over.

00:25:12.444 --> 00:25:14.036
Set a pursuit course.

00:25:14.112 --> 00:25:15.079
Yes, ma'am.

00:25:18.149 --> 00:25:20.743
The photon torpedoes you gave me
are worthless.

00:25:20.819 --> 00:25:21.820
No better than plasma flares.

00:25:21.820 --> 00:25:23.219
No better than plasma flares.

00:25:23.288 --> 00:25:24.846
Perhaps you
didn't arm them properly.

00:25:24.923 --> 00:25:26.322
And in the middle of the battle,

00:25:26.391 --> 00:25:29.451
the Polonians warned me
to cease hostilities

00:25:29.528 --> 00:25:33.225
or face destruction
at the hands of your Federation!

00:25:33.298 --> 00:25:35.357
You allowed my enemies
to join!

00:25:35.433 --> 00:25:37.731
Evidently, the Federation
Council decided that...

00:25:37.802 --> 00:25:40.066
Your Federation is a fraud!

00:25:40.138 --> 00:25:42.436
I demand reparations.

00:25:42.507 --> 00:25:44.668
You will have to submit
a formal report to Starfleet.

00:25:44.743 --> 00:25:45.937
Enough!

00:25:46.044 --> 00:25:50.242
If you will not reimburse me,
I'll seize your ship.

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:55.479
Disable the beam!

00:25:58.089 --> 00:25:59.181
I can't.

00:25:59.257 --> 00:26:01.782
We have an additional problem...

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:02.827
Voyager.

00:26:04.563 --> 00:26:06.997
There's another ship
alongside the impostors.

00:26:07.065 --> 00:26:08.794
It's got them in a tractor beam.

00:26:08.867 --> 00:26:10.129
Hail both vessels.

00:26:12.604 --> 00:26:14.663
No response from either one.

00:26:14.739 --> 00:26:16.001
Well, let's try to
get their attention.

00:26:16.074 --> 00:26:17.041
Mr. Tuvok...

00:26:18.143 --> 00:26:20.043
Voyager's charging weapons.

00:26:20.111 --> 00:26:21.806
Perhaps we should
surrender to them.

00:26:21.880 --> 00:26:24.075
The Federation has an
extremely humane policy

00:26:24.149 --> 00:26:25.514
regarding the treatment

00:26:25.584 --> 00:26:27.575
of prisoners...

00:26:27.652 --> 00:26:30.485
Hail Varn again!

00:26:30.555 --> 00:26:32.614
Do it!

00:26:32.691 --> 00:26:34.556
Look on your scanners, Varn.

00:26:34.626 --> 00:26:36.685
Our mothership's arrived.

00:26:36.761 --> 00:26:38.422
She's armed
and ready to defend us.

00:26:38.496 --> 00:26:41.192
Tell them to stand down.

00:26:43.234 --> 00:26:47.603
Release us,
or Voyager will destroy you.

00:26:47.672 --> 00:26:49.435
The other ship is hailing.

00:26:49.507 --> 00:26:51.532
On screen.

00:26:52.210 --> 00:26:54.940
Stand down, Voyager.

00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:56.547
I have no argument with you.

00:26:56.615 --> 00:26:58.742
However, the vessel
you're tractoring...

00:26:58.817 --> 00:27:00.341
I paid
for my Federation membership.

00:27:00.418 --> 00:27:03.319
The Delta Flyer
belongs to me now.

00:27:03.388 --> 00:27:06.221
Sir, I think
you've been misled.

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:09.021
Yes, I have.

00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:17.131
Three direct hits.

00:27:17.202 --> 00:27:18.692
Shields down to 60 percent.

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:19.998
Target his tractor beam.

00:27:20.071 --> 00:27:21.333
Nobody is taking possession

00:27:21.406 --> 00:27:23.237
of the "Delta Flyer"
today, except us.

00:27:27.679 --> 00:27:29.237
Lock on to them.

00:27:29.314 --> 00:27:30.440
Yes, ma'am.

00:27:32.283 --> 00:27:33.773
Now our tractor generator's
off-line.

00:27:33.852 --> 00:27:37.686
Shields down to 41 percent.

00:27:37.756 --> 00:27:41.283
The impostor's ship
is powering engines.

00:27:41.359 --> 00:27:42.348
Seven, transport everyone

00:27:42.427 --> 00:27:43.894
on that vessel
directly to the brig.

00:27:43.962 --> 00:27:47.454
Establishing a lock
on three life signs.

00:27:47.532 --> 00:27:49.523
That impact damaged
the transporters.

00:27:49.601 --> 00:27:51.262
I'm losing annular confinement.

00:27:51.336 --> 00:27:52.735
Harry, reroute
additional power!

00:27:57.709 --> 00:27:58.641
They're gone.

00:27:58.710 --> 00:27:59.642
Seven?

00:27:59.711 --> 00:28:01.542
I only got one of them.

00:28:01.613 --> 00:28:04.047
Get us out of here,
Mr. Paris.

00:28:04.115 --> 00:28:05.446
Aye, Captain.

00:28:26.971 --> 00:28:28.996
Nice hair.

00:28:29.074 --> 00:28:31.941
It's not really my taste.

00:28:34.179 --> 00:28:36.841
Posing as a Starfleet Captain,

00:28:36.915 --> 00:28:39.247
selling memberships
to the Federation...

00:28:39.317 --> 00:28:40.249
Too bad we didn't

00:28:40.318 --> 00:28:41.250
think of it, Tuvok.

00:28:41.319 --> 00:28:42.377
Imagine the resources

00:28:42.454 --> 00:28:44.786
we could have acquired
over the past six years.

00:28:44.856 --> 00:28:45.823
Indeed.

00:28:45.890 --> 00:28:46.857
I have to admit

00:28:46.925 --> 00:28:48.586
I'm impressed.

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:50.855
I wish I could say the same.

00:28:50.929 --> 00:28:52.920
The great Captain Janeway.

00:28:53.031 --> 00:28:54.862
Somehow, I expected you

00:28:54.933 --> 00:28:56.400
to be...

00:28:56.468 --> 00:28:58.629
taller.

00:28:58.703 --> 00:29:00.136
I make a better you than you.

00:29:00.205 --> 00:29:02.036
Oh, I don't know.

00:29:02.107 --> 00:29:04.974
I'd say we're
very much alike...

00:29:05.043 --> 00:29:08.706
resourceful, intelligent,
ambitious...

00:29:08.780 --> 00:29:12.272
but with just one
tiny difference.

00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:14.011
And what is that?

00:29:14.085 --> 00:29:16.110
I'm not a liar and a thief.

00:29:16.187 --> 00:29:18.121
You're going to give me

00:29:18.189 --> 00:29:20.350
a detailed account
of everyone you cheated

00:29:20.425 --> 00:29:22.791
and exactly what you did
with their property.

00:29:22.861 --> 00:29:25.523
Why would I do that?

00:29:25.597 --> 00:29:26.689
Because if you don't,

00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:29.097
I'm turning you over
to Telsian Security.

00:29:29.167 --> 00:29:32.261
Oh, is that supposed
to frighten me?

00:29:32.337 --> 00:29:34.464
How much do you know
about the Telsians?

00:29:34.539 --> 00:29:38.202
Just that they're a more
gullible species than most.

00:29:39.277 --> 00:29:42.644
Tell her about your
research, Mr. Tuvok.

00:29:43.915 --> 00:29:45.906
I-I beg your pardon, Captain?

00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:47.142
On Telsian law.

00:29:47.218 --> 00:29:48.879
I think it's only fair

00:29:48.953 --> 00:29:52.116
that we let our guest
know what to expect.

00:29:52.190 --> 00:29:57.594
The Telsian criminal justice
system is rather barbaric.

00:29:57.662 --> 00:30:01.257
Tell her about the prisons.

00:30:01.332 --> 00:30:02.924
Barely habitable.

00:30:03.067 --> 00:30:05.934
Inmates often die
of malnutrition

00:30:06.004 --> 00:30:08.199
before they are
brought to trial.

00:30:08.273 --> 00:30:10.707
Torture is commonplace,
as is disease,

00:30:10.775 --> 00:30:13.938
including several incurable
forms of psoriasis.

00:30:14.012 --> 00:30:16.276
I think she gets
the general idea.

00:30:17.382 --> 00:30:19.145
Suppose I do tell you.

00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:23.950
How do I know you won't turn me
over to the Telsians anyway?

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:27.957
If you make full restitution
to your victims,

00:30:28.059 --> 00:30:30.926
I'll give you safe passage
out of this area.

00:30:30.995 --> 00:30:34.192
Is that a promise, Captain?

00:30:34.265 --> 00:30:36.893
I know it's hard
for you to believe,

00:30:36.968 --> 00:30:40.335
but occasionally,
some of us tell the truth.

00:30:42.707 --> 00:30:43.867
Give me the Delta Flyer

00:30:43.942 --> 00:30:46.706
and three days to get
as far away from here as I can,

00:30:46.778 --> 00:30:50.270
and then I'll send you
the information you want.

00:30:50.348 --> 00:30:52.578
How naive do you think I am?

00:30:52.650 --> 00:30:55.517
As far as the victims
are concerned,

00:30:55.587 --> 00:30:58.283
you're the one who cheated them.

00:30:58.356 --> 00:30:59.550
Without my help,

00:30:59.624 --> 00:31:02.525
you'll be the one
who has a problem

00:31:02.594 --> 00:31:04.221
leaving this sector.

00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:10.734
Tuvok, contact
Telsian Security.

00:31:17.075 --> 00:31:20.044
Tell them we have
a prisoner to turn over.

00:31:28.519 --> 00:31:29.747
"Psoriasis"?

00:31:29.821 --> 00:31:32.381
Lmprovisation is not
foremost among my talents.

00:31:32.457 --> 00:31:34.288
Considering I caught you
off guard,

00:31:34.359 --> 00:31:36.623
I thought your performance
was exemplary.

00:31:36.694 --> 00:31:37.683
Thank you, Captain.

00:31:37.762 --> 00:31:39.627
Was your order
to call the Telsians

00:31:39.697 --> 00:31:40.823
part of the deception,

00:31:40.899 --> 00:31:43.299
or did you actually
want me to contact them?

00:31:43.368 --> 00:31:44.699
Not yet.

00:31:44.769 --> 00:31:46.669
Let's give Dala some time
to think about

00:31:46.738 --> 00:31:47.864
those barbaric prisons.

00:31:47.939 --> 00:31:49.236
Do you believe she'll relent?

00:31:49.307 --> 00:31:50.296
I'm not sure.

00:31:50.375 --> 00:31:51.433
Something tells me

00:31:51.509 --> 00:31:52.942
she's just as stubborn as I am.

00:31:53.011 --> 00:31:53.943
Then, am I to assume

00:31:54.012 --> 00:31:55.377
you have an alternative plan?

00:31:55.446 --> 00:31:58.108
I'm like you, Tuvok...
making it up as I go along.

00:32:13.031 --> 00:32:15.295
The Captain said
bread and water,

00:32:15.366 --> 00:32:17.834
but I didn't see any harm.

00:32:17.902 --> 00:32:19.301
I'm not hungry.

00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:27.442
I'll just leave it here...

00:32:27.512 --> 00:32:30.743
in case you change your mind.

00:32:35.019 --> 00:32:36.884
May I ask you something?

00:32:38.089 --> 00:32:41.058
You want to know if you really
resemble the Redeemer of Light?

00:32:41.125 --> 00:32:42.956
I'm not that gullible.

00:32:43.094 --> 00:32:44.652
Then what?

00:32:46.965 --> 00:32:49.195
Do you ever feel guilty?

00:32:50.702 --> 00:32:51.964
Taking advantage of people

00:32:52.103 --> 00:32:54.367
who actually think
that you care about them?

00:32:56.374 --> 00:32:58.399
You seem like a good person.

00:32:58.476 --> 00:33:00.205
I'm sorry I lied to you.

00:33:00.278 --> 00:33:04.442
Actually, I think you're
just sorry you got caught.

00:33:06.384 --> 00:33:08.045
Probably.

00:33:08.119 --> 00:33:09.313
There.

00:33:09.387 --> 00:33:10.718
Now you're being honest.

00:33:10.788 --> 00:33:12.881
I knew it was possible.

00:33:14.592 --> 00:33:17.356
If you don't mind my asking,

00:33:17.428 --> 00:33:20.124
why do you do what you do?

00:33:20.198 --> 00:33:24.862
My father taught me most people
will exploit you if they can.

00:33:24.936 --> 00:33:27.666
So, it's best
to exploit them first.

00:33:29.240 --> 00:33:32.937
You know, I used
to be a lot like you.

00:33:33.044 --> 00:33:34.944
Living by my wits,

00:33:35.013 --> 00:33:37.379
never trusting anyone,

00:33:37.448 --> 00:33:39.916
always, uh, trying to end up

00:33:39.984 --> 00:33:42.919
on the more profitable side
of a transaction.

00:33:42.987 --> 00:33:46.218
But now you don't hesitate
to help starving orphans.

00:33:46.290 --> 00:33:47.655
I changed...

00:33:47.725 --> 00:33:51.559
when Captain Janeway
made me part of her crew.

00:33:51.629 --> 00:33:54.962
I suppose you
suddenly reformed.

00:33:55.066 --> 00:33:56.966
No, no, not right away.

00:33:57.068 --> 00:34:00.868
At first, I was just
exploiting an opportunity

00:34:00.938 --> 00:34:04.806
to get a warm bed,
food, protection.

00:34:04.876 --> 00:34:07.401
I kept waiting to find out
what the Captain

00:34:07.478 --> 00:34:08.809
wanted in return.

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:11.405
But she never asked for a thing.

00:34:11.482 --> 00:34:12.779
On the contrary.

00:34:12.850 --> 00:34:15.614
She expected
a great deal from me.

00:34:15.686 --> 00:34:18.246
Honesty, loyalty, hard work.

00:34:18.322 --> 00:34:20.119
I should've guessed.

00:34:20.191 --> 00:34:24.184
But I discovered that
those were commodities

00:34:24.262 --> 00:34:26.924
I had in abundance,

00:34:27.031 --> 00:34:30.023
and i-it was much more
profitable to share them

00:34:30.101 --> 00:34:32.899
than it was to be self-serving
and cynical

00:34:32.970 --> 00:34:34.062
all the time.

00:34:34.138 --> 00:34:36.936
I-I-I'm happier than
I've ever been.

00:34:39.577 --> 00:34:42.478
I suppose that you think
I could change, too.

00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:45.380
Stranger things have happened.

00:34:46.984 --> 00:34:49.179
Do you really think
that she'll give me

00:34:49.253 --> 00:34:51.244
safe passage if I
make restitution?

00:34:51.322 --> 00:34:53.950
If that's what she promised you.

00:34:54.092 --> 00:34:55.081
Then what?

00:34:55.159 --> 00:34:58.492
I have never done anything else.

00:34:59.931 --> 00:35:02.900
Captain Janeway let
Seven of Nine

00:35:02.967 --> 00:35:04.366
remain on board,

00:35:04.435 --> 00:35:05.766
and she was Borg.

00:35:05.837 --> 00:35:08.806
Are you saying she'd do
the same thing for me?

00:35:08.873 --> 00:35:11.467
I'd be willing to talk to her.

00:35:11.542 --> 00:35:14.033
I cheated you.

00:35:14.112 --> 00:35:16.672
Why are you being so kind to me?

00:35:16.747 --> 00:35:20.615
Like my great-grandmother
used to say...

00:35:20.685 --> 00:35:23.085
"It's nice to be nice."

00:35:27.492 --> 00:35:29.084
Is that tea still warm?

00:35:39.704 --> 00:35:41.831
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm so clumsy.

00:35:47.712 --> 00:35:49.270
Security to the brig!

00:36:21.345 --> 00:36:23.176
She's gone.

00:36:33.391 --> 00:36:34.915
It's not right to abandon her.

00:36:34.992 --> 00:36:37.358
Going back is too dangerous.

00:36:37.428 --> 00:36:38.395
She's our Captain.

00:36:38.462 --> 00:36:39.690
No, she's not.

00:36:39.764 --> 00:36:40.924
And even if she were,

00:36:41.032 --> 00:36:42.363
we wouldn't be able
to rescue her.

00:36:42.433 --> 00:36:43.365
We'd be captured
ourselves.

00:36:43.434 --> 00:36:44.594
Without Captain Janeway,

00:36:44.669 --> 00:36:47.194
it will be difficult
to continue our activities.

00:36:47.271 --> 00:36:48.898
It's too late for that.

00:36:48.973 --> 00:36:50.941
There must be
a logical way...

00:36:51.008 --> 00:36:54.466
What's logical is to get
as far away as we can.

00:36:56.981 --> 00:36:59.381
There's a vessel
approaching.

00:36:59.450 --> 00:37:01.281
It's the Delta Flyer.

00:37:01.352 --> 00:37:03.013
Activate the shields.

00:37:03.087 --> 00:37:04.384
They're hailing.

00:37:05.456 --> 00:37:08.152
It's Captain Janeway.

00:37:08.226 --> 00:37:11.093
Our Janeway or theirs?

00:37:11.162 --> 00:37:12.561
Which one did you expect?

00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:15.326
I'm pleased to see you, Captain.

00:37:15.399 --> 00:37:17.026
Lower the shields,
so I can transport aboard.

00:37:17.101 --> 00:37:20.537
How were you able to escape?

00:37:20.605 --> 00:37:22.266
I'll tell you once I'm aboard.

00:37:22.340 --> 00:37:24.467
It's difficult to believe
you weren't detected.

00:37:24.542 --> 00:37:26.806
Are you accusing me
of something?

00:37:34.819 --> 00:37:36.081
...being cautious.

00:37:36.153 --> 00:37:40.021
How do we know
this isn't a deception?

00:37:40.091 --> 00:37:41.922
Why would I try to deceive you?

00:37:42.026 --> 00:37:44.551
You could be helping Voyager
capture us in exchange...

00:37:44.629 --> 00:37:46.096
Are we in position?

00:37:46.163 --> 00:37:47.323
We don't have time for this.

00:37:47.398 --> 00:37:48.330
- Lower your shields...
- Ready?

00:37:48.399 --> 00:37:50.367
And beam me aboard.

00:37:56.674 --> 00:37:59.040
Captain on the Bridge.

00:37:59.110 --> 00:38:01.237
A-As you were.

00:38:02.446 --> 00:38:04.710
Now...

00:38:04.782 --> 00:38:06.682
what about the bolomite
and the rest of our earnings?

00:38:06.751 --> 00:38:09.117
They're exactly
where we left them.

00:38:09.186 --> 00:38:11.814
Well, it's time to collect
them and leave the region.

00:38:11.889 --> 00:38:13.754
Set a course before
Voyager finds us.

00:38:13.824 --> 00:38:15.883
You're not in command here.

00:38:15.993 --> 00:38:19.156
I just spent the last
24 hours in Voyager's brig.

00:38:19.230 --> 00:38:21.391
I have no intention
of going back.

00:38:21.465 --> 00:38:23.626
I'm picking up life signs

00:38:23.701 --> 00:38:24.895
on the Delta Flyer.

00:38:25.036 --> 00:38:26.333
That can't be.

00:38:29.573 --> 00:38:30.597
I was right.

00:38:30.675 --> 00:38:31.835
You brought them here.

00:38:31.909 --> 00:38:33.467
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

00:38:33.544 --> 00:38:35.774
Whoever it is
must've stowed away.

00:38:35.846 --> 00:38:37.473
They're hailing.

00:38:37.548 --> 00:38:39.641
On screen.

00:38:39.717 --> 00:38:41.878
This is Tom Paris
of the Starship Voyager.

00:38:41.952 --> 00:38:43.112
Prepare to be boarded.

00:38:44.388 --> 00:38:45.685
He's charging weapons.

00:38:45.756 --> 00:38:46.950
Evasive maneuvers.

00:38:59.437 --> 00:39:00.802
Let's get everything
on board

00:39:00.871 --> 00:39:01.860
as quickly as we can.

00:39:01.939 --> 00:39:03.770
How many transport enhancers

00:39:03.841 --> 00:39:05.536
do you recommend, Captain?

00:39:05.609 --> 00:39:07.474
Do I have to think
of everything?

00:39:07.545 --> 00:39:08.773
We'll need at least ten

00:39:08.846 --> 00:39:11.110
if we're going to beam
all that bolomite

00:39:11.182 --> 00:39:12.376
through the geostrata.

00:39:12.450 --> 00:39:14.350
Maybe we should take 12.

00:39:14.418 --> 00:39:15.612
"We"?

00:39:15.686 --> 00:39:17.881
Is there a problem?

00:39:17.955 --> 00:39:20.150
In six years,
I've never known you

00:39:20.224 --> 00:39:22.886
to dirty your hands
with menial labor.

00:39:22.960 --> 00:39:26.896
Well, there's a first time
for everything.

00:39:26.997 --> 00:39:28.157
You don't trust us.

00:39:28.232 --> 00:39:30.496
Who knows what
the two of you planned

00:39:30.568 --> 00:39:32.399
while I was in Voyager's brig.

00:39:32.470 --> 00:39:33.903
As Chief of Security,
I would never...

00:39:33.971 --> 00:39:36.030
It's all right.

00:39:36.107 --> 00:39:37.938
We'll all go together.

00:39:39.377 --> 00:39:41.368
After you.

00:39:52.089 --> 00:39:55.456
The next populated sector
is 13 days from here.

00:39:55.526 --> 00:39:59.394
When we arrive, we'll trade
the Delta Flyer for a new ship.

00:39:59.463 --> 00:40:01.294
Voyager will never find us.

00:40:01.365 --> 00:40:04.027
Are all the transport
enhancers in place?

00:40:04.101 --> 00:40:06.069
That's the last of them.

00:40:06.137 --> 00:40:07.468
We can go now...

00:40:07.538 --> 00:40:10.564
if that's acceptable
to you, Captain.

00:40:10.641 --> 00:40:11.938
I'm afraid there's been

00:40:12.009 --> 00:40:13.306
a change of plans.

00:40:14.979 --> 00:40:16.776
I've found the stolen items,
Captain.

00:40:16.847 --> 00:40:18.542
You can lock on
to my coordinates.

00:40:18.616 --> 00:40:20.709
I told you
she couldn't be trusted.

00:40:20.785 --> 00:40:24.050
How could you bring yourself
to deceive your fellow officers?

00:40:24.121 --> 00:40:26.589
Voyager, I repeat,
I am in position.

00:40:26.657 --> 00:40:27.715
Can you get a lock?

00:40:27.792 --> 00:40:28.816
Voyager, trans...

00:40:28.893 --> 00:40:30.417
Negative.
The geostratum is too dense.

00:40:30.494 --> 00:40:31.586
Keep trying.

00:40:31.662 --> 00:40:33.254
Please respond immediately.

00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:34.319
I'm outnumbered.

00:40:34.398 --> 00:40:35.422
Tuvok.

00:40:35.499 --> 00:40:36.796
Captain, I need assistance.

00:40:36.867 --> 00:40:38.596
Voyager, now would be
an excellent time

00:40:38.669 --> 00:40:39.636
to initiate transport.

00:40:39.703 --> 00:40:42.001
You're not transporting
anything.

00:40:46.610 --> 00:40:48.339
Captain?

00:40:56.353 --> 00:40:58.184
Voyager, please respond.

00:41:00.458 --> 00:41:02.688
You're a sight for sore eyes.

00:41:07.698 --> 00:41:11.099
Commander... Tuvok.

00:41:11.168 --> 00:41:12.760
The one and only.

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:17.832
Logic would indicate

00:41:17.908 --> 00:41:20.900
that neither of us
has the advantage.

00:41:20.978 --> 00:41:23.572
Your logic is flawed.

00:41:27.852 --> 00:41:30.320
Stay where you are.

00:41:33.657 --> 00:41:36.524
What did they promise you
for betraying us?

00:41:36.594 --> 00:41:41.088
I believe you've mistaken me
for someone else.

00:41:43.267 --> 00:41:45.292
Where's Dala?

00:41:45.369 --> 00:41:48.429
I'm afraid she's indisposed
at the moment.

00:41:51.408 --> 00:41:54.571
I wouldn't get up too fast
if I were you, Captain.

00:41:54.645 --> 00:41:56.977
It's going to take
another few minutes

00:41:57.114 --> 00:41:59.082
for the ambizine to wear off.

00:42:01.919 --> 00:42:05.446
Captain's Log, Stardate 53849.2.

00:42:05.523 --> 00:42:09.015
The stolen property has been
returned to the Telsian miners,

00:42:09.093 --> 00:42:12.153
as well as vessels
from seven different worlds.

00:42:12.229 --> 00:42:15.130
I'm hoping that the reputation
of the real Federation

00:42:15.199 --> 00:42:18.691
will survive the events
of the last several days.

00:42:18.769 --> 00:42:21.169
'Round and 'round they go.

00:42:21.238 --> 00:42:22.933
Follow the terra nut if you can.

00:42:23.073 --> 00:42:24.597
But remember, the hand

00:42:24.675 --> 00:42:27.109
is sharper than
your visual acuity.

00:42:27.177 --> 00:42:30.112
I thought we'd already
disproved that theory.

00:42:30.180 --> 00:42:32.011
You tell me.

00:42:34.184 --> 00:42:36.175
The terra nut
is firmly entrenched

00:42:36.253 --> 00:42:37.550
up your right sleeve.

00:42:40.491 --> 00:42:41.753
Sorry.

00:42:47.264 --> 00:42:48.322
That's impossible.

00:42:48.399 --> 00:42:50.196
The old handoff.

00:42:53.170 --> 00:42:54.159
Ooh.

00:42:54.238 --> 00:42:56.001
That's cheating.

00:42:58.042 --> 00:42:59.509
We've still got it.
